    [Performance] enable torch.compile for the deepseek V4.1 (#18081)
    
    - Decorate DeepseekV41Model with @support_torch_compile so the V4.1
    backbone is captured by vLLM's compile path. It was the only DeepSeek
    model in vllm_ascend left undecorated: deepseek_v4/model.py and
    deepseek_v41/dspark.py already opt in. Without the decorator the
    backbone stays outside FX-graph compilation, so the npugraph_ex passes
    and the static-shape kernel optimization never apply to it.
    - Mark dim 0 of input_ids, positions and intermediate_tensors as
    dynamic. Dim 0 is the token dimension for all three (the forward uses
    positions.shape[0] as the token count), so the compiled graph stays
    reusable across batch sizes instead of re-specializing per shape.
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
